// # Port Session - Stateful Rust-Parity Scene Driver
//
// Logline: Holds one ported scene's state across preview frames so intro animation and settle match the Rust lifecycle.
// Setup: Pure state threading over the tests/oo bit-exact scene ports. Operates with zero ambient authority.
// Beats:
//   1. Build canvas geometry for the terminal size and construct every ported scene state.
//   2. Continuous ports step their World each call; run ports replay their bit-exact frame tape frame-by-frame.
//   3. A scene that has played out holds its settled frame, the way the Rust reference reports a finished scene and leaves the settled frame standing until the next scene is chosen.
//   4. Render the latest frame through the arcade composite pipeline (starfield, gleam, settled banner).

